2026-08-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2140) 'OpenBao on FoundationDB
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2140) 'Restore the FoundationDB backend from Vault v1.14.8 (last MPL-2.0 release), connecting to the existing weftspun-fdb cluster over 6PN. The port rewrites three interfaces that diverged after the fork: `ListPage`, interactive transactions (`BeginTx`/`BeginReadOnlyTx` with Commit/Rollback), and pins the FDB 7.3.79 Go binding (`headerVersion = 730`). Build tag `foundationdb`, `CGO_ENABLED=1`.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2140) 'Deployment files in weftspun/service-openbao. Bao runs beside the FDB server on each weftspun-fdb machine (RFD66606-2353) and reaches the cluster as a TLS client. Interface details and deploy measurements are in DETAILS.md.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2140) 'Verification
 # tags: rfd:section-heading
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2140) '`bao status`: Storage foundationdb, unsealed. KV v2 at `secret/`, anchor creds written from weftspun-fdb over 6PN. Root in 1Password.
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2140) 'RFD66606-2109 (FDB as the store), RFD66606-2134 (cluster TLS).
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2140) 'The three interface changes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2140) 'OpenBao's `physical.Backend` diverged from Vault's after v1.14.x. The port rewrites three sites.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2140) '**ListPage.** Vault's `List(prefix)` returned all keys. OpenBao added `ListPage(ctx, prefix, after, limit)` to the interface. The FDB implementation uses a range query with `after` as a begin-selector offset and `limit` as the range option.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2140) '**Interactive transactions.** Vault used a one-shot `Transaction([]*TxnEntry)`. OpenBao replaced it with `BeginTx` and `BeginReadOnlyTx`, each returning a `physical.Transaction` carrying Put/Get/Delete/List/ListPage/Commit/Rollback. The FDB port calls `db.CreateTransaction()` and wraps the result in a struct that tracks committed/readonly state and returns the canonical error sentinels (`ErrTransactionReadOnly`, `ErrTransactionAlreadyCommitted`, `ErrTransactionCommitFailure`). PostgreSQL's `transaction.go` was the reference for the shape.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2140) '**Backend registry.** `internal/command/commands.go` gains one import and one map entry (`"foundationdb": physFDB.NewFDBBackend`), wired the same way file, inmem, raft, and postgresql are.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2140) 'The binding version
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2140) 'The FDB Go binding hardcodes a `headerVersion` that must match or exceed the C client's API version. The 2019 binding (`cd5c9d91fad2`, headerVersion around 520) crashed at startup with error 2203 against the FDB 7.3 C client. The 7.3.79 binding (`0074653ee011`, `headerVersion := 730`) resolved it. The Go pseudo- version is `v0.0.0-20260715201227-0074653ee011`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2140) 'The deploy
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2140) 'Since 2026-10-13 Bao runs on the three `weftspun-fdb` machines, one HA instance beside each FDB server, at 512 MB each (RFD66606-2353). The image layers the Bao image's binaries and plugins onto the FDB server image, so the plugin catalog's hashes still match. Bao reads the server's own cluster file and presents the machine's FDB leaf as its client certificate, so it verifies the cluster with the rule the cluster uses.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2140) 'Listener binds `[::]:8200` (dual-stack). Each instance advertises its machine address (`<machine-id>.vm.weftspun-fdb.internal`) as `api_addr` and `cluster_addr`, so standbys forward to the active instance. Clients verify the listener as `weftspun-bao.internal`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2140) 'The first deploy was a separate `weftspun-bao` app on one machine, built by `Dockerfile.fdb` with only the FDB client library. That app is stopped and kept for rollback until the operator retires it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2140) 'What the co-located fdbserver was, and why it moved
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2140) 'The first deploy ran a single-node fdbserver inside the bao machine on the same volume. That worked for initialization but carried no redundancy, no backup, and no TLS. Moving to the cluster gives all three for free. The co-located entrypoint and the single-node config are kept in the repository's git history.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2140) 'What the anchor creds cover
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2140) 'Two KV v2 paths carry the FDB cluster's identity material:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2140) '`secret/fdb/tls-anchor`: the CA certificate (base64 PEM), the cluster ID, and the verify-peers rule.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2140) '`secret/fdb/blobstore`: the Tigris S3 credentials used by the FDB backup agents (AWS key pair, endpoint, region, bucket name).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2140) 'Both were written from a weftspun-fdb machine over 6PN, where the Fly secrets are available as environment variables.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2140) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2140) 'The weftspun-fdb cluster already runs three machines with double redundancy, TLS, and backup, and raft on a single shared-cpu machine has no replication path.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2140  1 LINE
 Text:Written

